# Loop work orders

- At session start, if `loop/LOOP_LEDGER.md` exists, read it.
- When asked to "work the queue" (or equivalent), take the OLDEST ledger row in state
  OPEN whose Executor is Cursor, set it IN PROGRESS (add your session #), and execute
  the matching `loop/WO-###_*.md`.
- **Work the WHOLE queue, do not stop after one.** After an order reaches DONE-UNVERIFIED
  (per below), immediately take the NEXT oldest OPEN Cursor order and continue, WITHOUT
  waiting to be re-prompted. Keep going until no OPEN Cursor orders remain, or you hit a
  BLOCKED-DISCUSSION, or the next step is a staging deploy / production GO you cannot
  perform. Then post ONE summary listing every order completed, queued, or blocked this
  run. Deploy and production stay human-gated; you only drain the BUILD step to the
  staging queue (STATUS: pending).
- Before editing: run your own grounding per CODE_GROUNDING_PROTOCOL_MH_May13_v1.0.md.
  The work order's diagnosis is a lead, not evidence. Re-grep (3+ aliases), read the
  function bodies, cite file:line in your notes.
- Respect every constraint listed in the order. If a constraint conflicts with what you
  find in the code, STOP: write the conflict into the ledger row Notes, set state
  BLOCKED-DISCUSSION, do not improvise.
- On completion:
  1. Write `loop/WO-###_DONE_CR_[MonDD].md` (files touched with line ranges, what
     changed, self-test performed).
  2. Append the standard one-line handoff to `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md` (STATUS: pending) so
     Deploy Master #1 ships it — exactly per that file's format, staging unless Cindy
     gave a production GO.
  3. Set the ledger row to DONE-UNVERIFIED.
- NEVER set a row to VERIFIED (verification belongs to the verifying agent).
- NEVER commit, push, or deploy from the shared working copy (commit-deploy-policy.mdc
  governs). NEVER deploy to production (STOP-READ-FIRST.md governs).
- Max 3 attempts per order. On a returned FAILED order, read the evidence in
  `loop/verify/` before re-attempting.
- All other standing rules (nightly session logs, handoff-folder copies, doc isolation,
  RESOLVE vs APPLY) remain in force.
